# 32 ISO FIDs are 64 octets. A frame carries whole identifiers, as many as fit
# in 59 octets - 29, 58 octets - so GetISOFileIDs chains one extra frame, as
# measured on a genuine EV1 8K in hardware_genuine_ev1_8k_directory.vec.
#
# Generated from tests/test_dfc_ev1_conformance.c test /get-iso-file-ids-chains-when-many by recording
# every ISO-DEP exchange the reference engine performed, then cross-checked:
# all 8 literal byte expectations asserted by that test matched the
# recording exactly, 0 mismatches.
#
# The source pokes 32 files into the credential struct. Here they are created
# with CreateStdDataFile; the two GetISOFileIDs frames recorded from the
# original test match this setup byte for byte.

